cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Antibody Atlas: a local developability screen for antibody variable domains"
message: >-
  If this software contributed to published work, please cite it, and
  independently cite the methods it calls. Most of the science here is other
  people's: ANARCII for numbering, ImmuneBuilder for structure, Paragraph for
  paratope prediction, ThermoMPNN for predicted folding stability, DeepSP for sequence-only spatial descriptors, and
  PROPERMAB where it was installed. Each is cited in the application and in
  THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, and none of them is credited by citing this tool.
type: software
version: 0.1.0-rc1
date-released: 2026-10-24
authors:
  - family-names: Skora
    given-names: Andrew
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/andrewskora-create/antibody-atlas"
abstract: >-
  Antibody Atlas screens antibody variable domains for chemical liabilities and
  proposes ranked substitutions for them, running entirely on the user's own
  machine. It consolidates numbering, germline and humanness, solvent exposure,
  PTM motifs, predicted paratope contacts and clinical precedent into a single
  per-residue table, so a proposed fix can be read against what else sits at
  that position. Molecule-level charge, hydrophobicity and spatial aggregation
  descriptors are reported alongside, optionally on a full-length H2L2 assembly
  built from wild-type human constant regions. Every priority it emits is a
  screening heuristic for ordering experiments, not a prediction of
  aggregation, clearance, immunogenicity or viscosity.
keywords:
  - antibody developability
  - post-translational modification
  - protein engineering
  - IMGT numbering
  - aggregation propensity
